\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Effect of model parasitism heterogeneity on the stability of the Murdoch 1987. n is the number of subcompartiments, or the shape fo the Gamma distribution of maturation time. In case of $n \rightarrow \infty $, maturation time is fixed and parasitism risk is homogeneous over all hosts. k is the term of overdispersion of parasitism which is dispersed . In case of $k \rightarrow \infty $, parasitism is perfectly homogenenous over all hosts.\relax }}{10}\protected@file@percent }
